1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:03,311
Welcome to the Python for DevOps masterclass.

2
00:00:03,311 --> 00:00:04,311
Before any code,

3
00:00:04,311 --> 00:00:11,871
one habit that separates a script that works on your machine from a tool a whole team can trust: the virtual environment.

4
00:00:12,421 --> 00:00:14,075
Today: check your Python,

5
00:00:14,075 --> 00:00:15,993
create a virtual environment,

6
00:00:15,993 --> 00:00:17,184
install a package,

7
00:00:17,184 --> 00:00:20,426
record the exact versions in a requirements file,

8
00:00:20,426 --> 00:00:23,006
rebuild the environment from that file,

9
00:00:23,006 --> 00:00:24,858
and lay out a clean project.

10
00:00:25,408 --> 00:00:29,901
Every terminal demo is a real recording on Ubuntu twenty-four oh four,

11
00:00:29,901 --> 00:00:33,045
with real installs from the Python package index.

12
00:00:35,095 --> 00:00:40,215
Why not just install packages for the whole machine? Because Ubuntu itself uses Python.

13
00:00:40,765 --> 00:00:44,023
The system Python belongs to the operating system.

14
00:00:44,023 --> 00:00:45,978
Add or upgrade packages there,

15
00:00:45,978 --> 00:00:49,170
and you can break the tools the system relies on.

16
00:00:49,720 --> 00:00:54,055
Two projects can also need different versions of the same package.

17
00:00:54,055 --> 00:00:54,843
One machine,

18
00:00:54,843 --> 00:00:55,893
one global copy,

19
00:00:55,893 --> 00:00:57,272
so one of them loses.

20
00:00:57,822 --> 00:01:00,027
A virtual environment solves both.

21
00:01:00,027 --> 00:01:02,297
It is a folder inside your project,

22
00:01:02,297 --> 00:01:04,956
with its own Python and its own packages.

23
00:01:04,956 --> 00:01:06,123
Delete the folder,

24
00:01:06,123 --> 00:01:07,614
and everything is gone.

25
00:01:08,164 --> 00:01:09,987
The recipe has three parts.

26
00:01:09,987 --> 00:01:11,540
Create the environment.

27
00:01:11,540 --> 00:01:12,350
Activate it.

28
00:01:12,350 --> 00:01:13,430
Install into it.

29
00:01:13,430 --> 00:01:15,927
Then freeze the versions into a file,

30
00:01:15,927 --> 00:01:17,615
so anyone can rebuild it.

31
00:01:19,665 --> 00:01:23,889
First, check your Python. Type: python three, dash dash version.

32
00:01:24,439 --> 00:01:26,109
Python three point twelve,

33
00:01:26,109 --> 00:01:29,641
the version that ships with Ubuntu twenty-four oh four.

34
00:01:29,641 --> 00:01:31,439
Where does this Python live?

35
00:01:31,439 --> 00:01:32,852
Ask it for its prefix.

36
00:01:32,852 --> 00:01:34,072
Type: python three,

37
00:01:34,072 --> 00:01:34,521
dash C,

38
00:01:34,521 --> 00:01:37,026
then a line that prints sys dot prefix.

39
00:01:37,576 --> 00:01:38,473
Slash U S R.

40
00:01:38,473 --> 00:01:40,416
That is the system Python,

41
00:01:40,416 --> 00:01:42,658
owned by the operating system,

42
00:01:42,658 --> 00:01:45,423
so we never install packages into it.

43
00:01:45,423 --> 00:01:47,067
Make a project folder.

44
00:01:47,067 --> 00:01:48,114
Type: M K dir,

45
00:01:48,114 --> 00:01:48,861
inventory.

46
00:01:49,411 --> 00:01:52,163
Go inside. Type: CD, inventory.

47
00:01:52,713 --> 00:01:55,332
Now create a virtual environment.

48
00:01:55,332 --> 00:01:56,839
Type: python three,

49
00:01:56,839 --> 00:01:57,395
dash M,

50
00:01:57,395 --> 00:01:57,871
V env,

51
00:01:57,871 --> 00:01:58,665
dot V env.

52
00:01:58,665 --> 00:01:59,696
Python three,

53
00:01:59,696 --> 00:02:00,252
dash M,

54
00:02:00,252 --> 00:02:00,728
V env,

55
00:02:00,728 --> 00:02:02,553
builds the environment,

56
00:02:02,553 --> 00:02:05,172
and dot V env is the folder name.

57
00:02:08,722 --> 00:02:14,247
It takes a few seconds. List the folder, including hidden files. Type: L S, dash A.

58
00:02:15,797 --> 00:02:19,904
A hidden folder called dot V env now sits inside the project.

59
00:02:19,904 --> 00:02:22,194
It holds a private copy of Python,

60
00:02:22,194 --> 00:02:24,416
and a private place for packages.

61
00:02:26,466 --> 00:02:32,119
Now turn the environment on. Type: source, dot V env, slash bin, slash activate.

62
00:02:33,169 --> 00:02:35,610
The prompt now starts with dot V env,

63
00:02:35,610 --> 00:02:36,402
in brackets.

64
00:02:36,402 --> 00:02:39,898
That is your reminder that the environment is active.

65
00:02:39,898 --> 00:02:41,217
Where is Python now?

66
00:02:41,217 --> 00:02:42,471
Type: which python.

67
00:02:43,021 --> 00:02:45,928
The path points inside the project folder.

68
00:02:45,928 --> 00:02:48,488
This is the Python you are using now.

69
00:02:48,488 --> 00:02:49,734
Install a package.

70
00:02:49,734 --> 00:02:50,426
Type: pip,

71
00:02:50,426 --> 00:02:50,980
install,

72
00:02:50,980 --> 00:02:51,464
dash Q,

73
00:02:51,464 --> 00:02:52,087
requests.

74
00:02:59,637 --> 00:03:00,983
Dash Q means quiet,

75
00:03:00,983 --> 00:03:02,966
so pip only prints problems.

76
00:03:02,966 --> 00:03:06,508
It fetched requests from the Python package index,

77
00:03:06,508 --> 00:03:07,570
called pie P I.

78
00:03:07,570 --> 00:03:09,199
List what is installed.

79
00:03:09,199 --> 00:03:10,261
Type: pip list.

80
00:03:11,811 --> 00:03:12,456
Requests,

81
00:03:12,456 --> 00:03:14,105
four packages it needs,

82
00:03:14,105 --> 00:03:15,538
called dependencies,

83
00:03:15,538 --> 00:03:16,613
and pip itself.

84
00:03:16,613 --> 00:03:17,975
Look closer at one.

85
00:03:17,975 --> 00:03:18,691
Type: pip,

86
00:03:18,691 --> 00:03:19,050
show,

87
00:03:19,050 --> 00:03:19,695
requests,

88
00:03:19,695 --> 00:03:20,053
pipe,

89
00:03:20,053 --> 00:03:20,411
grep,

90
00:03:20,411 --> 00:03:20,985
Version.

91
00:03:21,535 --> 00:03:22,718
The exact version.

92
00:03:22,718 --> 00:03:23,770
Versions matter,

93
00:03:23,770 --> 00:03:28,241
because the same code can behave differently on a different version.

94
00:03:28,241 --> 00:03:28,570
Next,

95
00:03:28,570 --> 00:03:29,556
we record them.

96
00:03:31,606 --> 00:03:35,745
To share exactly what you installed, freeze it. Type: pip, freeze.

97
00:03:36,295 --> 00:03:37,271
Every package,

98
00:03:37,271 --> 00:03:38,805
with an exact version,

99
00:03:38,805 --> 00:03:40,687
joined by two equals signs.

100
00:03:40,687 --> 00:03:42,291
This is called pinning.

101
00:03:42,291 --> 00:03:43,546
Save it to a file.

102
00:03:43,546 --> 00:03:44,243
Type: pip,

103
00:03:44,243 --> 00:03:44,731
freeze,

104
00:03:44,731 --> 00:03:47,729
then a redirect into requirements dot text.

105
00:03:48,279 --> 00:03:49,337
Nothing printed,

106
00:03:49,337 --> 00:03:51,851
because the output went into the file.

107
00:03:51,851 --> 00:03:52,776
Show the file.

108
00:03:52,776 --> 00:03:53,438
Type: cat,

109
00:03:53,438 --> 00:03:54,893
requirements dot text.

110
00:03:55,443 --> 00:03:56,851
The same five lines.

111
00:03:56,851 --> 00:04:00,019
This file is the recipe for your environment,

112
00:04:00,019 --> 00:04:01,567
and it belongs in Git.

113
00:04:01,567 --> 00:04:03,398
Now leave the environment.

114
00:04:03,398 --> 00:04:04,595
Type: deactivate.

115
00:04:05,145 --> 00:04:07,184
The prompt is back to normal.

116
00:04:07,184 --> 00:04:08,873
Now prove the isolation.

117
00:04:08,873 --> 00:04:11,897
Try to use requests from the system Python.

118
00:04:11,897 --> 00:04:13,234
Type: python three,

119
00:04:13,234 --> 00:04:13,726
dash C,

120
00:04:13,726 --> 00:04:14,851
import requests.

121
00:04:15,401 --> 00:04:17,082
No module named requests.

122
00:04:17,082 --> 00:04:19,167
The system Python never saw it.

123
00:04:19,167 --> 00:04:21,453
Each project has its own packages,

124
00:04:21,453 --> 00:04:23,807
and nothing leaks between projects.

125
00:04:25,857 --> 00:04:27,209
Now the real test.

126
00:04:27,209 --> 00:04:29,539
A teammate clones your project.

127
00:04:29,539 --> 00:04:31,192
They get no dot V env,

128
00:04:31,192 --> 00:04:32,394
only your files.

129
00:04:32,394 --> 00:04:33,596
List the folder.

130
00:04:33,596 --> 00:04:34,348
Type: L S.

131
00:04:34,898 --> 00:04:36,938
Just the requirements file.

132
00:04:36,938 --> 00:04:38,978
Create a fresh environment.

133
00:04:38,978 --> 00:04:40,413
Type: python three,

134
00:04:40,413 --> 00:04:40,942
dash M,

135
00:04:40,942 --> 00:04:41,395
V env,

136
00:04:41,395 --> 00:04:42,151
dot V env.

137
00:04:45,701 --> 00:04:50,309
Activate it. Type: source, dot V env, slash bin, slash activate.

138
00:04:50,859 --> 00:04:52,500
Install from the file.

139
00:04:52,500 --> 00:04:53,245
Type: pip,

140
00:04:53,245 --> 00:04:53,842
install,

141
00:04:53,842 --> 00:04:54,364
dash Q,

142
00:04:54,364 --> 00:04:54,886
dash R,

143
00:04:54,886 --> 00:04:56,527
requirements dot text.

144
00:04:56,527 --> 00:04:59,734
Dash R means: read the list from this file.

145
00:05:07,284 --> 00:05:10,291
Now compare what is installed with the file.

146
00:05:10,291 --> 00:05:10,975
Type: pip,

147
00:05:10,975 --> 00:05:11,453
freeze,

148
00:05:11,453 --> 00:05:11,795
pipe,

149
00:05:11,795 --> 00:05:12,137
diff,

150
00:05:12,137 --> 00:05:12,479
dash,

151
00:05:12,479 --> 00:05:13,982
requirements dot text.

152
00:05:14,532 --> 00:05:15,224
No output,

153
00:05:15,224 --> 00:05:17,024
which means no difference.

154
00:05:17,024 --> 00:05:18,547
Check the exit status.

155
00:05:18,547 --> 00:05:19,308
Type: echo,

156
00:05:19,308 --> 00:05:19,793
dollar,

157
00:05:19,793 --> 00:05:20,762
question mark.

158
00:05:21,312 --> 00:05:21,638
Zero.

159
00:05:21,638 --> 00:05:24,375
The new environment matches yours exactly.

160
00:05:24,375 --> 00:05:25,939
That is reproducibility,

161
00:05:25,939 --> 00:05:28,416
and it is the whole point of the file.

162
00:05:30,466 --> 00:05:32,336
Now the project structure.

163
00:05:32,336 --> 00:05:34,422
Code goes in a source folder,

164
00:05:34,422 --> 00:05:36,651
and tests go in a tests folder.

165
00:05:36,651 --> 00:05:37,658
Type: M K dir,

166
00:05:37,658 --> 00:05:38,162
dash P,

167
00:05:38,162 --> 00:05:39,816
source slash inventory,

168
00:05:39,816 --> 00:05:40,535
and tests.

169
00:05:41,085 --> 00:05:42,293
Add an init file,

170
00:05:42,293 --> 00:05:45,206
so Python treats the folder as a package.

171
00:05:45,206 --> 00:05:46,059
Type: touch,

172
00:05:46,059 --> 00:05:48,119
source slash inventory slash,

173
00:05:48,119 --> 00:05:48,474
init,

174
00:05:48,474 --> 00:05:49,043
dot P Y.

175
00:05:49,593 --> 00:05:52,078
Tell Git to ignore the environment.

176
00:05:52,078 --> 00:05:53,640
You commit the recipe,

177
00:05:53,640 --> 00:05:55,699
never the environment itself.

178
00:05:55,699 --> 00:05:56,480
Type: echo,

179
00:05:56,480 --> 00:05:57,616
dot V env slash,

180
00:05:57,616 --> 00:05:58,256
redirect,

181
00:05:58,256 --> 00:05:59,321
dot git ignore.

182
00:05:59,871 --> 00:06:01,086
Show the layout,

183
00:06:01,086 --> 00:06:02,529
skipping dot V env.

184
00:06:02,529 --> 00:06:03,364
Type: find,

185
00:06:03,364 --> 00:06:03,668
dot,

186
00:06:03,668 --> 00:06:04,427
dash path,

187
00:06:04,427 --> 00:06:05,946
dot slash dot V env,

188
00:06:05,946 --> 00:06:06,781
dash prune,

189
00:06:06,781 --> 00:06:07,313
dash O,

190
00:06:07,313 --> 00:06:08,148
dash print.

191
00:06:08,698 --> 00:06:10,910
That is the shape: requirements,

192
00:06:10,910 --> 00:06:11,394
source,

193
00:06:11,394 --> 00:06:11,808
tests,

194
00:06:11,808 --> 00:06:13,191
and the ignore file.

195
00:06:13,191 --> 00:06:14,573
Now run the checker,

196
00:06:14,573 --> 00:06:16,578
which comes with this lesson.

197
00:06:16,578 --> 00:06:17,338
Type: bash,

198
00:06:17,338 --> 00:06:18,306
dot dot slash,

199
00:06:18,306 --> 00:06:20,103
check forty-seven dot S H,

200
00:06:20,103 --> 00:06:20,794
and a dot.

201
00:06:21,344 --> 00:06:26,421
Five PASS lines. Your project is isolated, pinned, reproducible, and tidy.

202
00:06:28,471 --> 00:06:32,716
Cleanup, with proof. List the project first. Type: L S, dash A.

203
00:06:33,266 --> 00:06:36,082
Leave the folder. Type: CD, dot dot.

204
00:06:36,632 --> 00:06:42,478
Delete the whole project, environment included. Type: R M, dash R F, inventory.

205
00:06:43,028 --> 00:06:45,481
Now prove it is gone. Type: L S.

206
00:06:46,031 --> 00:06:47,931
Only the checker file is left.

207
00:06:47,931 --> 00:06:51,540
Removing a virtual environment is just deleting a folder.

208
00:06:51,540 --> 00:06:53,946
Nothing was installed into the system.

209
00:06:55,996 --> 00:06:57,081
Here is your task,

210
00:06:57,081 --> 00:06:58,589
with everything you need.

211
00:06:58,589 --> 00:07:00,518
The files are in the repository,

212
00:07:00,518 --> 00:07:01,905
and in the description.

213
00:07:02,455 --> 00:07:08,130
The repository is git hub dot com, slash it dash waves, slash dev ops dash A I.

214
00:07:08,680 --> 00:07:13,480
In the academy slash lesson forty-seven folder you will find the task file,

215
00:07:13,480 --> 00:07:14,504
and the checker,

216
00:07:14,504 --> 00:07:16,168
check forty-seven dot S H.

217
00:07:16,718 --> 00:07:21,654
You need an Ubuntu virtual machine with Python three and the venv package.

218
00:07:21,654 --> 00:07:22,321
On Ubuntu,

219
00:07:22,321 --> 00:07:25,657
that is the package called python three dash venv.

220
00:07:26,207 --> 00:07:31,711
Build a project called servers. Create the environment, install one package, and pin it.

221
00:07:32,261 --> 00:07:33,129
Add the layout,

222
00:07:33,129 --> 00:07:35,619
prove a fresh environment matches the file,

223
00:07:35,619 --> 00:07:36,546
run the checker,

224
00:07:36,546 --> 00:07:37,935
and clean up with proof.

225
00:07:38,485 --> 00:07:41,920
Write your results in a report, with the commands and their output.

226
00:07:43,970 --> 00:07:47,895
Here is how your work is judged. Six points, and you need all six.

227
00:07:48,445 --> 00:07:50,323
The checker shows five pass lines.

228
00:07:50,873 --> 00:07:53,731
The requirements file has exact, pinned versions.

229
00:07:54,281 --> 00:07:57,503
A fresh environment matches the file, with no difference.

230
00:07:58,053 --> 00:08:00,613
The environment folder is ignored by Git.

231
00:08:01,163 --> 00:08:03,509
The cleanup proof shows nothing left behind.

232
00:08:04,059 --> 00:08:08,795
You worked only in your own virtual machine, and never installed into the system Python.

233
00:08:09,345 --> 00:08:10,967
To pass, you need all six.

234
00:08:13,017 --> 00:08:15,854
Your turn, in your own Ubuntu virtual machine.

235
00:08:16,404 --> 00:08:19,626
One: make the servers folder, and create the environment.

236
00:08:20,176 --> 00:08:22,736
Two: activate it, and install one package.

237
00:08:23,286 --> 00:08:26,528
Three: freeze the versions into requirements dot text.

238
00:08:27,078 --> 00:08:29,596
Four: build the layout, and the ignore file.

239
00:08:30,146 --> 00:08:33,175
Five: make a fresh environment, and prove it matches.

240
00:08:33,725 --> 00:08:36,349
Six: run the checker, then clean up with proof.

241
